{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Damage Done and Follow the Reaper feel like natural next choices because they combine aggression with melody, which fits my repeated listening to In Flames and my interest in Advance And Vanquish.",
    "Vol. 3 and The End of Heartache offer the heavy riffs and memorable hooks I want, while Audioslave connects with the more accessible hard rock side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Silence in Black & White leans toward emo and post-hardcore when I want heavier riffs; sharing some intensity with my past choices is not enough.",
    "Testify, IV: Constitution of Treason, and Seasons have some appeal, but I would pass on them for now because other choices more closely match the balance of heaviness and melody I want."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some accessible rock seems to have been stretched into an interest in emo and post-hardcore, although that is not what I am seeking now.",
    "Aggression or heavy grooves alone seem to count too much; those qualities interest me most when the melodies and hooks also pull me in."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My several In Flames albums are a strong clue that melodic death metal deserves particular attention among the heavier choices.",
    "I can find an album appealing without choosing it now: I would prioritize Damage Done and The End of Heartache over the less compelling matches on this page."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The choices mostly understand my taste for heavy music with melody, but sometimes treat nearby styles or heaviness alone as equally strong matches."
}"}
